{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1951","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1951","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1951\",\"parent_revision\":\"a7cb382745e2ff1948f64638a62eacbfededb63d\",\"root_revision\":\"08fcbec5921792ac799cce6f10570026ae3998c1bcd93d199fdac26fdc302de0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /research-curator |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` (434 lines) |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/research-curator/references/validation-rules.md` |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` (validate mode section, lines 278-349) |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Bottleneck: Every `--validate all` run re-processes all entries unconditionally; cost grows linearly with research directory size\\n- Affects: Any workflow that runs `validate_research.py --validate all` (CI, pre-commit, manual curator runs)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` | `--skip-unchanged` flag; cache read/write logic in `main()`; updated `collect_files()` exclusion; updated `--json` summary schema |\\n| `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/validation-rules.md` | Document new `skipped` field in JSON output schema and `--skip-unchanged` flag behavior |\\n| `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` | Update validate mode script invocation example to document the new flag |\\n| `.gitignore` (or `research/.gitignore`) | Add `research/.validate-cache.json` to prevent accidental commit |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n6/10 \u2014 Performance optimization for a growing research directory (60+ entries confirmed). Value compounds with repository size. Not urgent; no correctness issue in current behavior.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Subsequent validate runs on unchanged trees complete in near-zero time\\n- Only modified entries are re-validated; unchanged entries are skipped with no checks run\\n- Cache is opt-in via `--skip-unchanged`; existing behavior is byte-identical when flag is absent\\n- Cold cache (deleted or absent) safely falls back to full validation\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `uv run .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py --skip-unchanged ./research/` on an unmodified directory exits 0 and reports all entries as skipped (zero validated, zero errors).\\n2. After modifying one research entry file, running with `--skip-unchanged` validates only that file; all others are reported as skipped.\\n3. Running without `--skip-unchanged` produces byte-identical output to the current script (no cache side effects \u2014 no file created, no file read).\\n4. `./research/.validate-cache.json` is created after the first `--skip-unchanged` run and contains one hash entry per processed file.\\n5. `collect_files()` never returns `.validate-cache.json` as a validation target.\\n6. `--json --skip-unchanged` output includes `\\\"skipped\\\": N` in the summary object.\\n7. Deleting `.validate-cache.json` and re-running `--skip-unchanged` re-validates all entries (cold cache = full check).\\n8. `uv run prek run --files .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` exits 0 after the change.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen `--skip-unchanged` is passed:\\n1. Each `.md` file's SHA-256 content hash is compared against `./research/.validate-cache.json` from the previous run.\\n2. Files whose hash matches the cached value are skipped; all validation checks are bypassed for those files.\\n3. Files with a new or absent cache entry are validated as normal.\\n4. After the run, the cache file is updated with current hashes for all processed files.\\n5. Summary output includes: `N skipped (unchanged)` alongside normal totals.\\n6. `--json --skip-unchanged` output includes `\\\"skipped\\\": N` in the summary object.\\n\\nWhen invoked without `--skip-unchanged`, behavior is byte-identical to the current script \u2014 no cache is read or written.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSmall \u2014 single file change to `validate_research.py` (~50-80 new lines for cache logic), one reference file update, one SKILL.md example update, one `.gitignore` line. No new external dependencies. Well-bounded integration points.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add git-based incremental cache to research-curator validate to skip unchanged entries** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md \u2014 pattern: Git-based incremental caching using git status --porcelain and git diff\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-26\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n6/10 \u2014 Useful performance optimization for a large and growing research directory (60+ entries confirmed). Value compounds with repository size; currently validate_research.py processes all files unconditionally on every invocation.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `--skip-unchanged` is passed:\\n1. Each `.md` file's SHA-256 content hash is compared against `./research/.validate-cache.json` from the previous run.\\n2. Files whose hash matches the cached value are skipped; all validation checks are bypassed for those files.\\n3. Files with a new or absent cache entry are validated as normal.\\n4. After the run, the cache file is updated with current hashes for all processed files.\\n5. Summary output includes: `N skipped (unchanged)` alongside normal totals.\\n6. `--json --skip-unchanged` output includes `\\\"skipped\\\": N` in the summary object.\\n\\nWhen invoked without `--skip-unchanged`, behavior is byte-identical to the current script \u2014 no cache is read or written.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py --skip-unchanged ./research/` on an unmodified directory exits 0 and reports all entries as skipped (zero validated, zero errors).\\n2. After modifying one research entry file, running with `--skip-unchanged` validates only that file; all others are reported as skipped.\\n3. Running without `--skip-unchanged` produces byte-identical output to the current script (no cache side effects \u2014 no file created, no file read).\\n4. `./research/.validate-cache.json` is created after the first `--skip-unchanged` run and contains one hash entry per processed file.\\n5. `collect_files()` never returns `.validate-cache.json` as a validation target.\\n6. `--json --skip-unchanged` output includes `\\\"skipped\\\": N` in the summary object.\\n7. Deleting `.validate-cache.json` and re-running `--skip-unchanged` re-validates all entries (cold cache = full check).\\n8. `uv run prek run --files .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` exits 0 after the change.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /research-curator |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` (434 lines) |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/research-curator/references/validation-rules.md` |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` (validate mode section, lines 278-349) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 single file change to `validate_research.py` (~50-80 new lines for cache logic), one reference file update, one SKILL.md example update, one `.gitignore` line. No new external dependencies. Well-bounded integration points.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` | `--skip-unchanged` flag; cache read/write logic in `main()`; updated `collect_files()` exclusion; updated `--json` summary schema |\\n| `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/validation-rules.md` | Document new `skipped` field in JSON output schema and `--skip-unchanged` flag behavior |\\n| `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` | Update validate mode script invocation example to document the new flag |\\n| `.gitignore` (or `research/.gitignore`) | Add `research/.validate-cache.json` to prevent accidental commit |\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\n**Cache key**: hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest() \u2014 stdlib only, no subprocess, no git dependency. The item title says git-based but SHA-256 of file content achieves the same cache invalidation guarantee with zero added dependencies.\\n\\n**Cache location**: {research_root}/.validate-cache.json \u2014 co-located with the research directory. Excluded from collect_files by filename check (same guard as README.md on line 364 of the current script).\\n\\n**Invalidation strategy**: Per-file content hash only. No TTL. A file is unchanged when sha256(current_bytes) == cached_hash. Cache is always rewritten after each run.\\n\\n**Atomic write**: Write to .validate-cache.json.tmp, then os.replace(tmp, final) \u2014 prevents partial write on crash.\\n\\n**Exit code**: Unchanged \u2014 exits 1 if any validated (non-skipped) entry has errors, exits 0 otherwise. An all-skipped run exits 0.\\n\\n**Open design question**: Should git hash-object be used instead of SHA-256 of content? Confirmation preferred before implementation begins.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Should `git hash-object` be used instead of SHA-256 of file content, for alignment with git's object model? SHA-256 achieves the same cache invalidation guarantee with zero subprocess dependency, but the item title says \\\"git-based\\\". Preferred approach should be confirmed before implementation begins.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Source |\\n|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item title + description |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | Single file change: validate_research.py + --skip-unchanged flag |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | Full script read (434 lines); no existing cache; integration points are collect_files() line 356 and main() line 374 |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | PEP 723 stdlib-only script; hashlib, json, os.replace all stdlib; no new external deps |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | validate_research.py, SKILL.md validate mode, validation-rules.md, research/ directory (60+ entries) all read |\\n\\nNo MISSING or BLOCKED conditions.\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs the /research-curator --validate skill orchestrator (or a developer running validate_research.py directly), I want unchanged research entries to be skipped during --validate all runs, so that re-validation of a large research directory only processes files that have changed since the last validation run.\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun `uv run .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py --json ./research/` twice in succession on an unchanged tree. Second run completes in measurably less wall-clock time and the JSON output includes a `cache_hit_count` field equal to the total entry count minus 0 (or near zero \u2014 only entries with uncommitted changes re-validated). Touch one entry file (e.g., `touch ./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md`) \u2014 third run reports `cache_hit_count` = (total - 1) and `revalidated: ['./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md']`. Cache file present at `~/.cache/research-curator/<hash>.json` and contains a `last_validated_commit_sha` field.\\n\\nSource: Tolaria research entry (./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md), Vault Caching and Performance \u2014 \\\"Same commit \u2192 re-parse only uncommitted changes via git status --porcelain. Different commit \u2192 git diff to find changed files \u2192 selective re-parse. No cache \u2192 full walkdir scan.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n## Rt Ica Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Source |\\n|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Skip re-validation of research entries unchanged since last run |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | Single file change: `validate_research.py` + `--skip-unchanged` flag; opt-in only, existing behavior unchanged |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | Script read (434 lines); integration points: `collect_files()` line 356 and `main()` line 374 identified |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | PEP 723 stdlib-only script; `hashlib`, `json`, `os.replace` all stdlib; no new external deps |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | `validate_research.py`, `SKILL.md` validate mode, `validation-rules.md`, `research/` directory (60+ entries) all confirmed |\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Acceptance criteria defined with exact commands |\\n\\nNo MISSING or BLOCKED conditions.\\n\\nOpen design question (does not block planning): Should `git hash-object` be used instead of SHA-256 of file content for cache keys? Item title says \\\"git-based\\\" but SHA-256 achieves identical invalidation semantics with zero subprocess dependency. Human confirmation preferred before implementation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` and the `--rerun all` path always re-process every entry from scratch. There is no cache of last-validated commit per entry, no `git status --porcelain` shortcut to find changed files, and no `git diff` to identify which entries have changed since the last run. The `./research/` directory now contains 30+ category subdirectories with hundreds of entries (visible from the `ls /home/user/claude_skills/research/` listing). Every `--validate all` run performs a full walk and re-validates entries that have not changed since their last successful validation.\\n\\nFile: `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` \u2014 no cache layer, no git-aware change detection. SKILL.md `--validate` section (lines 275-350) describes a full rescan with no incremental option.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`validate_research.py` writes a cache at `~/.cache/research-curator/<repo-hash>.json` recording, per entry path: `last_validated_commit_sha`, `last_validated_at`, `last_validation_result_hash`. On invocation:\\n\\n1. If cache exists for current HEAD: run `git status --porcelain ./research/` to find uncommitted changes; re-validate only those entries.\\n2. If cache exists at a different commit: run `git diff --name-only <cached_sha> HEAD -- ./research/` to enumerate changed entries; re-validate only those.\\n3. If no cache: full scan and populate cache.\\n\\nA `--no-cache` flag forces full rescan. A `--invalidate-cache` flag deletes the cache before running (matching Tolaria's \\\"Reload Vault\\\" disposability invariant).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Questions For Human\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Should `git hash-object` be used instead of SHA-256 of file content, for alignment with git's object model? SHA-256 achieves the same cache invalidation guarantee with zero subprocess dependency, but the item title says \\\"git-based\\\". Human confirmation of preferred approach before implementation begins.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4d4c34db54a2dabebefbf1cd2fbd8e267aa9224e59318c56dbe7bc6d04dcac14\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiJEIw\"}"}